  "body": "@junov  As discussed offline, when an OffscreenCanvas has a WebGLRenderingContext, the value of one of the WebGL attribute \"preserveDrawingBuffer\" has no impact on the \"transfer\" nature of OffscreenCanvas.transferToImageBitmap(). In terms of implementation, I am a bit hesitant between a silent failure (i.e. user can set preserveDrawingBuffer to be true but the underlying bitmap in webgl will still be gone) or an explicit JS exception message telling users that they did something wrong.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3628/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 20, 2018, 5:36 PM GMT (ea8dc8f)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/3628/5d091c2...ea8dc8f/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 20, 2018, 5:36 PM GMT (ea8dc8f)\">diff</a> )",
